  "hash_binding": "This evidence is finalized before root verification and is itself hashed in that receipt. The final attestation binds receipt bytes, final snapshot and evidence bytes without a circular self-hash. Each per-round evidence record binds only the state at its own round, so its research/tasks.json entry is expected to go stale once a later round edits that file.",
  "proof_route": [
    "isOpen_regular: the critical set is closed (isClosed_critical, from continuity of fderiv), so the regular set is its open complement",
    "left-hand side: S splits into the disjoint measurable pieces S inter R and S inter C, and on C the gradient vanishes so the integrand is zero there; lintegral_union then drops the critical part",
    "right-hand side: L10 makes surfaceMeasure (C inter level set) zero at almost every level, so ae_eq_set and Measure.restrict_congr_set identify the slice integral over S inter level set with the one over (S inter R) inter level set for almost every level",
    "middle: L9 applied to the open set R and the measurable subset S inter R gives both the identity and the AEMeasurable component there",
    "the same almost-everywhere equality transports the AEMeasurable component (AEMeasurable.congr) and joins the two right-hand integrals (lintegral_congr_ae)",
    "T3 and the WIP hole's statement: L11 at S = univ, simplified by Set.univ_inter; their LipschitzWith hypothesis is unused"
  ],
  "not_proved": [
    "the LIPSCHITZ coarea formula Analysis.lintegral_enorm_gradient_mul_eq_lintegral_levelSet, still a direct hole; it assumes no C1 regularity and needs L12",
    "L12 (Lipschitz case), L7 (exact C1 pieces), L6/L6a (closed-set Whitney first-order jet extension and compact jet extraction)",
    "migration of KLS.Isoperimetry.lintegral_enorm_gradient_mul_eq_lintegral_levelSet out of WIP",
    "sharp C^(finrank) Analysis.sard (no downstream consumer) and Analysis.ae_forall_fderiv_ne_zero, both still carrying sorryAx",
    "sharpness of the Eilenberg constant",
    "smoothConstant_le_minkowskiConstant",
    "smoothConstant_mul_lintegral_min_superlevel_le",
    "equality of the two Cheeger constants"
  ],
